        "original_id": "c9c4239b-13ea-56dd-bf5e-bc488a8c37d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Characters: Space Ghost, Brak, Zorak, Moltar\n- People: Andy Merrill, C. Martin Croker, Don Messick\n- Series and Productions: Space Ghost's Musical Bar-B-Que, Space Ghost, Space Ghost Coast to Coast, Cartoon Planet\n- Companies: Hanna-Barbera, Cartoon Network\n- Roles: voice actor, television writer, producer, supervillain, space pirate\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1966 Hanna-Barbera animated series \"Space Ghost,\" Brak is a fictional catlike alien space pirate and supervillain who tries to conquer the galaxy.\n- Don Messick originally voiced Zorak and Moltar in the 1960s series \"Space Ghost.\"\n- Andy Ronald Merrill was born on November 27, 1966, in Newark, Ohio.\n- Andy Merrill is an American television writer, producer, and voice actor best known for his comedy voice portrayal of Brak on \"Space Ghost Coast to Coast,\" \"Cartoon Planet,\" and related Cartoon Network productions using \"Space Ghost\" characters.\n- C. Martin Croker was best known for voicing Zorak and Moltar on the animated series \"Space Ghost Coast to Coast,\" replacing Don Messick from the original 1960s series.\n- \"Space Ghost's Musical Bar-B-Que\" features songs and skits by Space Ghost and his arch enemies Zorak and Brak.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
